                                      rows-processed field counts 1, 2, 3
                                      rather than repeating the per-call
                                      count, and then a past-the-end
                                      answer that is the ordinary summary
                                      object carrying 1403 with
                                      "ORA-01403: no data found" and its
                                      newline behind it as a ub1-length
                                      string - 59 payload bytes, ending
                                      on the message with nothing after
                                      it.  before the fix that same call
                                      answered 115 bytes that parsed as
                                      no object at all, which cost the
                                      client the call and surfaced on the
                                      next one as ORA-03120 (#9976,
                                      #9702)
    9700-redhat9x86-portable-selectint-sqlrelay.oraproxy
